# Line endings. Almost everything here runs in Linux: inside the guest, inside a
# Docker container, or under bash. A checkout with core.autocrlf=true (common on
# Windows) would otherwise turn these into CRLF and break them in confusing ways
# ("$'\r': command not found", patches that do not apply). Force LF for all of it.
# tools/check-lf.py fails loudly if a CRLF slips in anyway; build.sh runs it first.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts are fine either way; keep them CRLF-friendly for PowerShell.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary (none are committed today; listed so a future one is never mangled).
*.png binary
*.icns binary
*.img binary
*.gz binary
*.cpio binary
*.ko binary
*.so binary
